Do not build the vmwgfx (KMS and 3D) path on illumos.

It needs the vmwgfx kernel DRM driver, which illumos does not have, and
configure enables it whenever Mesa's xatracker is installed, which then
also requires libudev. Build the legacy driver only, as before.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -89,6 +89,12 @@
                  [Has version 1.7.0 or greater of the Xserver])
 		 BUILD_VMWGFX=yes],[BUILD_VMWGFX=no])
 
+case $host_os in
+    solaris*)
+	BUILD_VMWGFX=no
+	;;
+esac
+
 PKG_CHECK_EXISTS([xorg-server >= 1.12.0],
                  [AC_DEFINE([HAVE_XORG_SERVER_1_12_0], 1,
                  [Has version 1.12.0 or greater of the Xserver])])
